replies.body:
All procedural. 

The same spec that places the parts also places the bones root → body → head / abdomen / jaws / palps... there's one chain per leg pair and however many legs I ask for.

Pistons in the legs get their own bones. A barrel on one segment and a rod on the next aimed at each other so they appear to slide as the joint bends. It's just a trick of the chrome that makes it look like it's moving. 

For authoring there's an IK controk rig on top that the blender cips are animated through. 

In unreal, every frame solves for each leg. The gait, body lean, bites and dodges and foot digs are all based on math in real time. 

Every frame it solves each leg:

- the coxa yaws like a turret toward the foot target;
- femur and tibia are solved as two-bone IK in the leg plane;
- the lower leg keeps its rest attitude, and the foot curls;
- pistons re-aim so their barrels and rods stay engaged.
